## Migration Strategy

### Phase V Rollout Plan

**Stage 1: Database Migrations (Week 1)**
- Deploy migrations 001-008 to staging
- Verify backward compatibility
- Deploy to production during low-traffic window

**Stage 2: Deploy New Services (Week 2)**
- Deploy Recurrence Service (no traffic yet)
- Deploy Reminder Service (no traffic yet)
- Verify health checks and Dapr connectivity

**Stage 3: Enable Features Gradually (Week 3)**
- Enable priorities and tags (low risk)
- Enable full-text search
- Monitor performance and Kafka throughput

**Stage 4: Enable Recurring Tasks (Week 4)**
- Enable recurrence pattern creation
- Monitor Cron trigger processing
- Verify event publishing

**Stage 5: Enable Reminders (Week 5)**
- Enable reminder scheduling
- Verify notifications working
- Monitor Kafka lag

**Stage 6: Full Rollout (Week 6)**
- All features enabled for all users
- Monitor metrics and alerts
- Optimize based on production data

---

## Testing Strategy

### Unit Tests

```python
# backend/tests/test_recurrence_processor.py
import pytest
from datetime import datetime, timedelta
from src.recurrence.processor import RecurrenceProcessor

@pytest.mark.asyncio
async def test_daily_recurrence_spawning(db_session, event_publisher):
    processor = RecurrenceProcessor(db_session, event_publisher)

    # Create daily recurrence pattern
    pattern = RecurrencePattern(
        task_id=1,
        user_id="user123",
        frequency="daily",
        interval=1,
        next_occurrence=datetime.utcnow() - timedelta(minutes=5)
    )
    db_session.add(pattern)
    await db_session.commit()

    # Process recurrences
    spawned = await processor.process_due_recurrences()

    assert spawned == 1
    assert pattern.occurrences_count == 1
    assert pattern.next_occurrence > datetime.utcnow()
```

### Integration Tests

```python
# backend/tests/integration/test_event_publishing.py
import pytest
from testcontainers.kafka import KafkaContainer

@pytest.mark.integration
async def test_task_creation_publishes_event():
    with KafkaContainer() as kafka:
        # Configure Dapr to use test Kafka
        # Create task via API
        response = await client.post("/api/todos", json={
            "title": "Test task",
            "priority": "high"
        })

        # Consume event from Kafka
        consumer = kafka.get_consumer("task-events")
        event = next(consumer)

        assert event["event_type"] == "task.created"
        assert event["data"]["priority"] == "high"
```

### E2E Tests

```typescript
// frontend/tests/e2e/recurring-tasks.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('create recurring task and verify spawning', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/todos');

  // Create recurring task
  await page.click('button:has-text("Add Task")');
  await page.fill('input[name="title"]', 'Weekly meeting');
  await page.check('input[name="recurring"]');
  await page.selectOption('select[name="frequency"]', 'weekly');
  await page.click('button:has-text("Save")');

  // Verify task created
  await expect(page.locator('text=Weekly meeting')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('text=Recurs weekly')).toBeVisible();

  // Wait for next occurrence (in test, mock cron to run immediately)
  await page.waitForTimeout(2000);

  // Verify new instance spawned
  const taskCount = await page.locator('text=Weekly meeting').count();
  expect(taskCount).toBe(2);
});
```

